From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 02/14] Plutonium: Exo: embedded windows

Exo's side of embedding: windows parked off the desktop until a page shows them, the page alone sizing them, focus, keyboard and pointer for embedded windows (pointer lock and confine, modal dialogs, popups), drag and drop, input methods, and window icons.

It holds these changes:
- report Wayland client pid through the window broker
- windowBroker.showOnDesktop to pop an embedded window out
- keep windows off the desktop, wl_output v4, embed input logs
- windowBroker.close() and snapshot() for the agent bridge
- parked windows don't occlude the page
- pointer capture (lock, confine) for embedded apps, Super+Escape
- niri shell keys, touchpad and scrolling, drag and drop, shell links as tabs
- the page alone sizes an embedded window
- agent keyboard focus beside the user's; the compositor decorates every window
- embedded focus follows modal dialogs (xdg_dialog_v1)
- a parked window's popups show only where a page shows it
- an agent sees and uses a window's popups
- an input method composes and commits into embedded windows
- keys an input method passes on reach every app
- a Wayland client's overlay priority hint doesn't crash Ash
- agents type through the session's keymap, and a temporary one for what it lacks
- xdg_toplevel_icon_v1, apps' window icons for the shells
- a parked window stays invisible when Ash demotes it
- Caps Lock, as Ash makes it, reaches apps as Escape
- Pluto Vim for native apps: keys held for the helper's engine, and given back in order

and the parts in these files of:
- Exo embedding (Phase 1) and window broker (Phase 2)
- shell mode on DRM, evdev input fix, display-plane path
- native fullscreen for embedded apps and tabs, Super+F, shell shortcuts
- object-fit and a resize cross-fade for <native-window>
- windowrequest events, and which element drives a window
- the switcher: shell pages, fullscreen windows, backup terminal and browser
- agents drive windows and tabs over DevTools
- shm buffers the GPU can't import don't stall the display; EXO-DIAG logs at VLOG(1)
- screen capture for shells, capture requests to the focused shell
- several displays, a shell per display, one window in one place
- ext-image-copy-capture-v1 in Exo, for grim
- a shell's MediaStream of a window is its surface tree's own frames
- zwp_text_input_v3 in Exo, for GTK 4, Qt 6 and foot
- xdg_activation_v1, apps raise their windows through the shell
- wp_cursor_shape_v1, cursors by name for GTK 4, Qt 6 and foot
- ext_idle_notify_v1, apps hear when the user is idle
- ext_data_control_v1, the clipboard for clipboard managers
- a floating native window keeps its client-side resize edges
- Super+F maximizes in the shell, Super+Shift+F is fullscreen; menus over a fullscreen element; a backdrop for presented windows
